        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A woman's bonnet veil,  1840s-1860s, British; warp-frame knitted blue silk, open pattern, lace-like edging"@en , "A bonnet veil of warp-frame knitted blue silk, in the shape of a wide semi-circle.  It is worked in a pattern of lace-like open stitches with a narrow border with picots along the straight edge, and a wider border of scalloped, floral motifs along the curved edge."@en ;
